I have explored fine-tuning different foundational models (inc. Gemini Flash) on both real-world and synthetic examples of aider's SEARCH and REPLACE blocks (~500 examples) and but have not had time to perform a statistical analysis on whether the fine tuned model made a real-world different. Furthermore, I have not tried a hold-out test example set yet either.

It does not help that litellm does not support gemini ai-studio fine-tuned models nor non-gemini models on VertexAI. This makes it hard to use Aider with these models once created. 

One other promising alternative would be to use formal `structured output` ([docs](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/structured-output?lang=python)) and have a programmatic translation layer from the structured JSON to aider's search and replace blocks.

